A milestone file is matched by develop's per-instance `milestone` artifact alone, so no
`--playbook` is needed: the instance is the milestone directory's name, the workdir the plan
directory the pattern hangs off, and the edge's hook regenerates that plan's milestone table.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan/index.md --
---
title: Plan
status: in-progress
sp: 0
---
# Plan

## Milestones

## Out of scope
-- fixtures/cwd/plan/milestones/M01-first/M01-first.md --
---
id: "01"
title: First
sp: 2
status: pending
plan: plans/plan/index.md
---
# M01: First
-- cmd --
booping transition plan/milestones/M01-first/M01-first.md in-progress
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
pending → in-progress
frontmatter: status=in-progress
script refresh-milestone-table: ok
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/plan/milestones/M01-first/M01-first.md --
---
id: "01"
title: First
sp: 2
status: in-progress
plan: plans/plan/index.md
---
# M01: First
